MCPair licences

Software (MIT)

The MIT License in LICENSES/MIT.txt covers the project's Python and C++
source files and the machine-readable physics checklist in
evidence/settings-source/checklist.json.

Research materials (CC BY 4.0)

Shiyang Zhang licenses the project's original documentation, input decks,
setting records, research data and figures under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International Public License, to the extent that copyright
or database rights apply. For attribution, cite Shiyang Zhang, MCPair, and
identify the version you used. The full terms are in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
and at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en.

Third-party material

The following files are archived outputs of the authors' CERN FLUKA 4-5.2
run. They are outside both project licence grants.

    evidence/example/formal-g000-f00/fluka/input001.out
    evidence/example/formal-g000-f00/fluka/input001_fort.21

The files retain their original notices. Third-party text quoted within
other records, including native FLUKA output excerpts, also remains outside
the project licence grants. The grants cover the authors' contributions
to those records and to the derived data and figures.

The simulation software is distributed separately by its developers.
For CERN's FLUKA software terms and required references, see
https://fluka.cern/download/licences,
https://fluka.cern/download/licences/fluka-single-user-licence and
https://fluka.cern/documentation/references.
